WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.860
- During my time at McKinsey,

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.040
I helped in designing
the training programs

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.970
for the new consultants.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:08.610
In these training programs,

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:13.570
communication was always one
of the most important skills.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.780
It was common feedback of
all the senior consultants

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.480
and all the partners
that the number one topic

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.310
where young consultants needed training on

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.150
and where they need to be
developed by the training programs

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.810
is how to communicate effectively.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:32.510
How to say the things in the right way.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.670
One of the most fundamental
concepts that we taught

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.030
in these training programs is the concept

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.120
of top-down communication.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.670
In this video, I'm going to talk

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:45.480
about what top-down communication is.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.680
We are jointly going to
work through one exercise

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.010
that I trust will really teach you

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:53.210
how top-down communication works.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.570
So by watching this video,

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.358
I trust that you will build
a very important skill set

00:00:57.358 --> 00:00:59.310
that will hugely benefit you,

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.840
not only if you work in consulting,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.450
but pretty much in every other role

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:05.930
in the professional context,

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.930
and probably even in your
private life as well.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.760
Welcome to another coffee break

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:14.230
with me here on my channel, Firm Learning.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:16.050
If you're new here with this channel,

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.408
I want to help you to become successful

00:01:18.408 --> 00:01:21.130
in the first years in your career.

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.930
But now without further
ado, let's jump into it.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.270
I will teach you how to
talk like a consultant.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:30.080
And this video will be
structured in two parts.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.230
First, I'm going to talk

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.700
about what top-down
communication actually is.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:36.800
And then second, we're going
to do an exercise together

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.050
to really help you engrain
this principle in your head.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.454
So what is top-down communication?

00:01:42.454 --> 00:01:45.747
And if you read all the books
and articles about that,

00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:48.870
you will find out that there
are lots of definitions.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.230
Many people claiming different things

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:53.060
to be top-down communication.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:56.190
So I really want to simplify it for you.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.810
So in my experience,

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:01.080
what this really comes
down to is two things.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.240
Namely, first in your communication
to focus on the results,

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.090
to focus on the content.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.840
To only focus on the things

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.690
that really matter to your audience.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:14.430
And second, always
starting your communication

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.810
with the key message, with the key result

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.270
that you want to communicate
to your audience.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.680
When people talk about
top-down communication,

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.180
they often also use the
word pyramid principle.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.070
The reason why you talk about a pyramid

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.030
where you have a pyramid structure

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:33.394
is because you need to imagine
and structure in your head

00:02:33.394 --> 00:02:37.220
all the different facts,
information, all the details

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:40.530
that you want to talk
about in a pyramidal form.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:44.570
So at the bottom, there are
all the underlying arguments,

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:46.100
there are the details.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.640
But then based on this fundament,

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.660
you would then draw some conclusions,

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.430
you would then draw some results.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:55.540
And then on the very
top is the key message

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:56.980
that you really wanna share

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.560
and that you really wanna talk about

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.140
and the main error that many people do

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.290
is not starting with this
result, with this key message,

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.340
but rather starting with
all the individual details,

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.420
with all the little arguments

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.770
that then your whole case is composed of,

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.020
and then only in the very end

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.110
to then draw the conclusion from it.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.750
So they pretty much
turn the pyramid around

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.810
and this for many different reasons

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:23.950
is not considered effective communication.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.750
And if you want to learn more about that,

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.130
I talked a lot about
this in my first video

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:29.890
in communication skills.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.080
I will link it somewhere
above here for you

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.180
if you want to check it out.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.770
So hopefully this clarifies
what top-down communication is,

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.050
but now to make it even
more tangible for you,

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:42.420
let's deep dive into a practical example.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.260
And this was an exercise that we did a lot

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.490
with young consultants, that
we used a lot at McKinsey

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:51.360
to train consultants in the organization.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.460
And you can imagine the overall setting

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.860
to be something like this:

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:58.140
You as a consultant
sitting in the team room,

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.740
just mind your business doing your work,

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.850
and then suddenly the CEO of the company

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.240
or another senior client of the company,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.830
or maybe even a partner is
walking into your team room

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.640
and asking you, "Hey,
Heinrich, how is it going?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.200
Where do we stand? What's
the current status?"

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.390
And this is a question

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.890
that hits many people kind of off guard

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.390
because you were just in the middle

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.570
of something completely else.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.780
And now you are required to

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:28.240
in front of a senior person
really concisely, briefly,

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.070
and to the point answering such a question

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.210
of where you stand with a specific task.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.610
So now let's jump into this exercise

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.250
and let's imagine you finding
yourself in such a situation,

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.800
and the context is as follows

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.160
and I'm reading from the slide here.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.230
So you are working on a market entry study

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.590
and the objective of the study is

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:53.440
to assess market entry opportunities
for a new product line.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.520
So the client tasked you to work on that.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.130
And of course it could easily also

00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:00.310
be just the internal team, so
not necessarily a consultant,

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.930
but an employee of the company

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.660
working on this specific task.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:06.360
And now in order to do that,
you conducted interviews

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:10.240
with lots of different
internal and external experts

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:11.950
to learn more about this topic.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.060
You analyzed lots of data,

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:15.640
you worked with different departments,

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:19.080
with the finance department,
with the marketing department.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.790
Probably the preliminary result,

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.910
the first indication that you have is

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:26.670
that the market entry in
France would be a good fit

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.450
and you're basing this result just based

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.410
on all these interviews that you conducted

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.360
and all these data analysis that you did.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.580
And now, indeed, the CEO walks in

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:38.250
and asks you to give a project summary.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.330
He says, "Hey, how is it going?

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:43.160
You work on the market
entry project, right?

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.110
What is the status on that?"

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:49.060
And now the question is,
how do you answer to that?

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.390
And now I just want to take you a moment

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:53.160
and ideally just grab a pen,

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.534
grab a piece of paper and just
jot down a couple of thoughts

00:05:56.534 --> 00:05:58.930
on how you would reply to that.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:05:59.770
And of course, if you want,

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:02.390
you can just briefly pause
the video to do that.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:05.050
Okay, so I hope to do just exactly that.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:08.480
And now I want to guide
you through two examples,

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:11.230
or two examples of potential answers.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:12.710
And then let's briefly discuss

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:15.250
what is going well with this example,

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:16.960
and maybe what isn't so much.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:19.040
Let's start with example number one

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:22.170
as a potential answer that
somebody could have given.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:24.117
And this answer goes as follows.

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:27.380
"So the last weeks we have
been very busy on the project.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:31.150
First, I talked to Tom from
finance to get the market data.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:33.190
However, when looking at the numbers,

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:36.400
we realized that marketing
has the better numbers,

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.420
with the new marketing data set

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:40.350
together with interviews we conducted,

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.800
we were able to get a good overview

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.140
of the different market opportunities.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:48.120
At the moment, it looks like
France will be a good fit

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:52.220
for our project, though this
is still work in progress."

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.650
So this could be an answer

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:56.610
and, from my experience, this is an answer

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:59.980
that many people would
give in such a situation.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.580
So let's just dissect it a bit.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.867
What is special? What is
characteristic about this answer?

00:07:04.867 --> 00:07:07.400
And this answer consists of the stating

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.290
all the different steps that you did,

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:12.100
all the different steps that you did

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:14.030
to come to this conclusion.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.750
Just saying, okay, first I
did that, then I did this.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:19.300
Then I talked to this guy,
then I talked to that guy.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:23.250
So lots of work that I put in,
I crunched all these numbers.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:28.000
And in the end, there is a
specific result that we have now.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.620
And of course now, if you look
into this, this is something

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:33.720
that you would not consider
talk-down communication.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.410
Okay guys, this is not
top-down communication

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:39.370
but it's the opposite, it's
bottom up communication

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:41.970
because you start by
giving all the details,

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:45.320
by giving all the nitty-gritty facts

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.430
and steps and arguments.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:51.380
This is communication that
is based on the process.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:53.940
It's based on the things that you did,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.360
but not so much about the result,

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:57.580
and in a business setting,

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:01.670
in most cases you want to
avoid communicate like that.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:05.520
And the main reason is that,
frankly, the CEO won't care,

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.850
the CEO will not care to whom you talk to,

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:11.380
whose data set you analyzed.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.000
These are all just details

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.800
that in most cases are
just not of interest,

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.220
but instead he will just trust you

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:19.950
that if you tell him something,

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.000
of course you will have done the research,

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.930
of course you will have done the analysis,

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:26.380
but in general, this
is just not the answer

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:29.550
that C-level executives of
companies are interested in.

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:32.420
Let's contrast this now
with a second example

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:35.040
of how such a question
could have been answered.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.220
And again, let me just
read it out for you.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:38.927
So, here, an answer could go like this:

00:08:38.927 --> 00:08:41.610
"Our current hypothesis is that France

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:43.950
would be the best fit for our project.

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:46.230
This is based on three reasons.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.590
First, our consumer research shows

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:51.640
that French consumers would
appreciate our offering.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.630
Second, the competitive
landscape in France

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.330
is not yet developed.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:58.890
We will be the first with this offering.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:02.810
Third, our logistics and
distribution capabilities

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:06.290
are well set up to serve
the French market."

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:08.510
And now, again, let's first dissect this.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.760
What is special about this answer?

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:14.150
So first, this answer
now doesn't talk at all

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.630
about the little steps in between

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:19.010
that you took to get to a result.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:22.970
Instead, this answer starts
by giving the result,

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:26.370
it starts by sharing
your current hypothesis.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.720
And so pretty much if
the CEO would need now

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.060
to leave the meeting just
after a couple of seconds,

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:34.000
if now would have a phone
call popping up on his phone

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.410
and he wouldn't be able to
now continue listening to you,

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:40.170
he already just with the first
sentences of your answer,

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.400
he would already know the result,

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:44.087
he would already know
what your hypothesis is.

00:09:44.087 --> 00:09:46.110
And of course now, if
he would have the time

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.680
to continue listening to you,

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.570
he would not only have the answer,

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:53.220
but he also also would be able
to hear the top three reasons

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.080
that you based your the conclusion,

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:57.390
that you based your answer on.

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:00.600
And this of course now is
information that the CEO

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.380
or other senior level executives

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.350
in the corporation will be interested in.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:08.110
This is the type of
communication that is top-down.

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:11.600
It focuses on the content or
for the results that you work,

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:13.330
but not on the process.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:16.560
This is exactly what top-down
communication is all about.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:18.710
And I would always encourage you

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:21.630
to communicate your
results in this fashion.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:23.880
So why is it so difficult for many people

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:27.730
to on-the-spot embrace this
top-down communication skill

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.470
and just communicate in that way?

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:31.820
Probably this is for three reasons.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:35.020
First, it's just the natural
way to talk about it,

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:36.970
to use this bottom-up approach, right?

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:40.090
It's just the order of
how you did the things.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:42.890
First you did this this, then
this, then this, then this.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:45.990
So this is just a natural way
of how you tell something.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.500
But, of course, still,
it's not the best way.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.660
So only because this
is your first impulse,

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:53.460
take a second, take a step
back and just reflect.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.630
The second reason why
I believe many people

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.560
rather use bottom-up than
top-down communication

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:02.790
is because it really stresses
all the work that you did.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:07.280
It shows all your sweat, all
the things, all the long hours

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:09.850
all the mental energy
that you put into a task.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:13.630
But the CEO will not care how
long you worked last night

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:16.700
or how smart you were by
coming up with the idea

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.670
of now hitting up the marketing guy.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:21.320
This is not what will interest
the senior-level guys.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.170
They will care about the results

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:25.310
so don't bore them with the process.

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:26.690
Don't try to impress them

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:28.530
with the long hours that you worked.

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:29.850
And the third reason is

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:32.040
that people are messy
in their head, right?

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:36.590
People for themselves often
do not have it crystal clear

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.480
why they are recommending something.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:41.440
What the underlying reasons
are when you come up

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:43.400
with a conclusion or
with a recommendation,

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.360
and so make sure just also for
the quality of the thinking,

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.110
for the quality of your documents,

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:50.920
that it's always crystal
clear for yourself,

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:51.890
just to start with,

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.100
what really the result is that
you want to put out there,

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:58.140
and what also the main
underlying arguments are

00:11:58.140 --> 00:11:59.910
that are supporting your conclusions.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.210
So I hope this video
helped you to understand

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:04.610
what top-down communication is all about.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:07.480
If you have any more
questions on this topic,

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:10.450
leave me a comment below
